{"version":"0.12.31","prev_tag":"v0.12.30","target":"default","tag_prefix":"","area_scope":[],"commits":[{"sha":"76f0879faef6926c170bf7e25067fdffdf405cb7","title":"Make bare lf a general-purpose conversation and add lf operate (#1393)","files":["README.md","docs/getting-started.md","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/LOOPFLOW.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/default.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/loopflow.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/ops/skill/repo_operate.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/wave/skill/review-open-work.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/prompt.rs","rust/loopflow/src/engine/skills.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/run.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/discovery.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/default_conversation_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/terminal_control_tests.rs","tests/goldens/basic.md","tests/goldens/builtin_debug.md","tests/goldens/builtin_implement.md","tests/goldens/builtin_realign.md","tests/goldens/with_docs.md"]},{"sha":"0713854d5359ab83e724d936fa3dffeafb43252e","title":"Make Doctor diagnose machine commands and keep cron working across installs (#1402)","files":["README.md","docs/architecture/environment.md","docs/conducting.md","docs/lf-reference.md","docs/troubleshooting.md","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/doctor.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/install/published.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/cron.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/doctor_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/global_commands.rs"]},{"sha":"fac48dd22ba8f98dc45174549cb1e281ce340db8","title":"Fix Codex Flow decisions and release completion after CI repair (#1401)","files":["TESTING.md","docs/architecture/planning.md","docs/authoring.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/flow_output.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/release.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/release_tests.rs"]},{"sha":"f889f071bbd27ad4a7e37230e272ebe7f6da827c","title":"Make Doctor diagnose broken Homes without changing their schema (#1404)","files":["docs/troubleshooting.md","rust/loopflow/src/bin/lf.rs","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/doctor.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/doctor_tests.rs"]},{"sha":"2064555c4418e153474505a19379189692dcaa21","title":"Advance Tasks with task/operate and open blocking Sessions in Desktop (#1405)","files":["README.md","rust/loopflow/src/engine/builtins/task/skill/task_operate.md","swift/LoopflowMac/PodiumModel.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/SessionsView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/WorkspacePalette.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/WorkspaceDestination.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/WorkspaceDestinationTests.swift","swift/README.md"]},{"sha":"101a19b8c5008705a6a527779c6fd6666f0c2637","title":"Keep current Tasks visible and browse completed history inline (#1403)","files":["docs/reviews/task-history.md","rust/loopflow/src/lf/commands/waves.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/chapter_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/planning_lookup_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/task_comments_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/pm/task_planning_tests.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_actions.rs","rust/loopflow/src/ops/task_flow.rs","rust/loopflow/src/pm/linear.rs","rust/loopflow/src/pm/mod.rs","rust/loopflow/src/store/sqlite/planning.rs","rust/loopflow/tests/dto_fixtures.rs","swift/Loopflow/Models/TaskStatus.swift","swift/Loopflow/Models/WaveWorkMap.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/MockWaveFixture.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/PodiumModel.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/TaskHistoryFilter.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/RoadmapView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/WaveDetailPane.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/Views/WorkSurfaceView.swift","swift/LoopflowMac/WorkspaceProjection.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/DTOFixtureTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/RegistryQueryTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/TaskHistoryFilterTests.swift","swift/LoopflowTests/WaveLensTests.swift","swift/README.md","tests/e2e/task_deletion.py","tests/fixtures/dto/pm_show.json","tests/fixtures/dto/roadmap_snapshot.json","tests/fixtures/dto/task_condition_states.json","tests/fixtures/dto/task_history_planning.json","tests/fixtures/dto/task_history_rows.json","tests/fixtures/dto/task_status.json","tests/fixtures/dto/wave_detail.json","wave/product/MEMORY.md"]},{"sha":"f4dfc620188aa16b78331c17e68cff2b00b32949","title":"Keep release publication compatible with the installed CLI (#1406)","files":["python/tests/test_release_publisher.py","scripts/publish_release.py","wave/infrastructure/MEMORY.md"]}],"merged_prs":[{"number":1393,"title":"Make bare lf a general-purpose conversation and add lf operate","body":"Bare `lf` previously opened a repository control conversation that checked Sessions on every turn and directed work elsewhere. It now follows the request and can work in the current checkout, with repository operations available explicitly through `lf operate`.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Add a lightweight default skill that answers questions and follows changing direction without requiring a repository inventory.\n- Consolidate the former `loopflow` and `review-open-work` skills into `repo/operate`, covering cleanup, activity summaries, Wave progression, and Task capture. The retired skill names are removed.\n- Resolve `lf operate` to `repo/operate`; keep `wave/operate` explicit and preserve repository skill overrides.\n- Keep bare `lf` in its launching terminal. Repository operation honors launch flags and configuration.\n- Update documentation and regression coverage for prompt separation, skill discovery, launch selection, and skill exports.\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded branch checks passed: skill export tests, the focused discovery test, `cargo fmt`, and `cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings`. These were not rerun for this description. The launch regression uses a simulated provider; it does not verify a live conversation.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough, not performed here: run `lf` and ask a question unrelated to repository management. The conversation should answer directly without first listing Sessions. Then run `lf operate` and request a summary of open work; it should inspect repository activity and identify useful next actions.","files":[],"additions":482,"deletions":411,"changed_files":19,"merge_commit":"76f0879faef6926c170bf7e25067fdffdf405cb7"},{"number":1401,"title":"Fix Codex Flow decisions and release completion after CI repair","body":"Codex could reject the Flow decision schema, and releases could stop on stale CI failures after repair and merge completed. Require nullable explanation fields in the provider schema while preserving historical receipts, and resume release settlement when fresh GitHub evidence confirms the merge.\n\nValidation: the new deterministic release regression failed before the repair and passed afterward. All 85 selected tests passed against the materialized migration schema: release_tests, pr_landing, Task completion, and Flow output. cargo fmt --all -- --check, cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings, and git diff --check passed. CI on the published head remains pending.","files":[],"additions":102,"deletions":15,"changed_files":6,"merge_commit":"fac48dd22ba8f98dc45174549cb1e281ce340db8"},{"number":1402,"title":"Make Doctor diagnose machine commands and keep cron working across installs","body":"Doctor treated valid machine-level Execs as corrupt history, while scheduled jobs could remain pinned to binaries retired by an installation change. This PR corrects that diagnosis, gives missing receipts actionable context, and makes newly reconciled jobs follow the stable machine entry gate.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Accept absent Exec repository scope; continue rejecting relative repository paths.\n- Include configured executable, log path, and Wave or repository reconciliation commands for missing scheduled receipts. Keep those failures visible.\n- Use the stable machine CLI gate for scheduled work and CI-watch installation; existing Sessions keep their runtime ownership.\n- Bound freshness output to three recent commits and direct installation to published releases.\n- Retain this branch's installation repair: download, promotion, rollback, and recovery no longer depend on Task PR authority; installation checks remain intact.\n\n## Checks\n\nDoctor unit tests (10), cron unit tests (16), Doctor CLI tests (3), installation regressions (2), local promotion tests (2), formatting, Clippy with warnings denied, and README/index sync passed.\n\nAn isolated replay of 3,990 unchanged production Execs reports valid identity, including 71 repository-free Execs, while preserving the two missing cron failures. The installed cron logs show startup refusal from a pinned inactive binary. Disposable gate replacement also preserves the installed job and produces a successful scheduled receipt.\n\n## Acceptance limits\n\nA full old-database copy was correctly rejected by the disposable Home's canonical-frontier contract; the history replay is not upgrade proof. Published upgrade and interrupted-switch recovery remain unverified. Live cron recovery requires installing a release containing this change, reconciling the jobs, and observing a real scheduled receipt. No release job was triggered merely to make Doctor pass.","files":[],"additions":216,"deletions":90,"changed_files":13,"merge_commit":"0713854d5359ab83e724d936fa3dffeafb43252e"},{"number":1403,"title":"Keep current Tasks visible and browse completed history inline","body":"Wave Task lists mixed current work with settled history, making unfinished Tasks harder to find. This PR shows current work by default and adds a compact control for browsing successful completions without hiding unresolved execution or losing access to retained Sessions.\n\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:start -->\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Task:** [Keep current Tasks visible and completed history out of the way · LOO-369](https://linear.app/loopflow/issue/LOO-369/keep-current-tasks-visible-and-completed-history-out-of-the-way)\n> **PR lifecycle:** Merging PR 1 completes the Task.\n<!-- loopflow:task-pr-context:end -->\n\n## What changes\n\n- Add a Completed control beside the Tasks heading and visible count. It starts with a seven-day range, supports inline editing, and remembers the range when toggled off. Entering 0 shows All Tasks, including successful completions of any age.\n- Keep settled canceled and duplicate Tasks out of completion history. Preserve visibility for unresolved execution and access to Tasks with retained Sessions.\n- Carry Linear workflow state and completion dates through storage and Rust/Swift projections. Unknown completion dates appear only in unbounded history; no dates are inferred.\n- Align Start availability and explanations with planning state so canceled, duplicate, and completed inventory cannot start new work.\n\n## Checks\n\nThe [recorded gate review](docs/reviews/task-history.md) reports 142 Rust tests and 100 selected headless Swift tests passing, plus formatting, all-target Clippy, architecture checks, Swift boundary checks, and signed Xcode build-for-testing. Coverage includes filtering, visible counts, actions, inline editing, and native glyph alignment. Checks were not rerun for this PR description.\n\nThe full test matrix remains with CI. Native visual/focus review, live Growth refresh, and real retained Session continuation remain unverified.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough: open a Wave containing current and completed Tasks. Click Completed to include the last seven days, click 7 Days and enter 30, then enter 0 for All Tasks. Rows and the heading count should follow the range while current work stays visible. Settled canceled and duplicate Tasks should remain absent. Enter an invalid range to confirm that validation preserves the previous selection; press Escape while editing to cancel.","files":[],"additions":2432,"deletions":79,"changed_files":37,"merge_commit":"101a19b8c5008705a6a527779c6fd6666f0c2637"},{"number":1404,"title":"Make Doctor diagnose broken Homes without changing their schema","body":"Doctor now inspects storage before ordinary startup admission, so missing or incompatible databases produce diagnostics without initialization or migration. Readable Exec evidence, scheduler obligations, and installation checks remain available when schema validation fails. Binary freshness uses cached origin/main and explicitly reports that limit, without fetching.\n\nValidated with six Doctor integration tests, twelve focused unit tests, cargo fmt, and cargo clippy --all-targets -- -D warnings. Tests cover absent and corrupt databases, future migration history, machine-scoped Execs, and telemetry continuity.\n\nThe supplied LOO-367 idle observation has since changed to running kickoff. This PR does not claim to repair its original launch timeout or missing scheduled invocations.","files":[],"additions":154,"deletions":51,"changed_files":4,"merge_commit":"f889f071bbd27ad4a7e37230e272ebe7f6da827c"},{"number":1405,"title":"Advance Tasks with task/operate and open blocking Sessions in Desktop","body":"Moving a Task forward required piecing together its Flow state and finding the conversation that needed attention. The new `task/operate` skill guides that work through completion or a concrete blocker, with a command to open the exact blocking Session in Loopflow Desktop.\n\n## What changes\n\n- Add `lf task/operate` instructions to read existing work, preserve unfinished Flows, resolve routine failures, and ask for judgment in the current conversation. Headless runs stop at blockers; review and delivery authority remain explicit.\n- Extend Task links with an optional `session` query that opens an existing conversation through Desktop’s normal Session-opening path, including Sessions found on later result pages.\n- Check Session membership against the runtime Task identity. Missing or unrelated Sessions preserve the current workspace and offer Retry.\n\n## Checks\n\nRecorded branch checks passed: 12 headless `WorkspaceDestinationTests`, builtin skill discovery, and built CLI help. No live Task was launched; the complete interactive workflow remains unverified.\n\n## Try it\n\nSuggested walkthrough, not performed: run `lf task/operate \"<issue>\"` for a Task awaiting review. When it reports the blocking Session, run the returned `open` command. Desktop should open that existing conversation in its terminal pane without completing the review or starting another Flow.","files":[],"additions":179,"deletions":6,"changed_files":8,"merge_commit":"2064555c4418e153474505a19379189692dcaa21"},{"number":1406,"title":"Keep release publication compatible with the installed CLI","body":"The v0.12.30 publisher stopped because the installed CLI rejects lf repo release publish. Use lf release publish for staging and finalization so the verified candidate can finish through the existing release operation. Also retain infrastructure acceptance evidence and the disposition of inactive development stores in Wave memory. Validation: six focused publisher tests passed; diff check passed.","files":[],"additions":58,"deletions":3,"changed_files":3,"merge_commit":"f4dfc620188aa16b78331c17e68cff2b00b32949"}],"decisions":null,"previous_release_notes":"# v0.12.30\n\n<!-- loopflow:release-notes=narrative;gate=safe -->\n\nv0.12.30 brings a Task’s conversations, terminals, files and Flow progress into one retained workspace, making it easier to return to work and find what needs a reply. Background checks keep enrolled Tasks moving, while CI watchers handle failed recorded landings. Context previews and usage reports expose what agents receive and where tokens and time go; operators should review the Home and command compatibility changes below before upgrading.\n\n## Return to the work, with its place preserved\n\nDesktop now keeps Task work together across visits. Shared checkout membership brings independently started conversations into the same view, while pending reviews and independent Flows remain protected during completion and cleanup.\n\n- Task workspaces retain Sessions, running shells, unfinished file drafts and split layouts when switching Tasks. Option-click opens a Session alongside another; hiding a pane keeps its process alive.\n- Browse checkout files and save revision-checked edits without a Project or PR. Files reached through symlinks remain read-only, and drafts survive access changes.\n- Use **⌘K** to find repository Waves, Tasks, Sessions and Flows, with recent destinations first. Search covers current Tasks and visited historical Tasks, not all Task history. `loopflow://task/ISSUE` links open details without starting work.\n- **Needs me** and `lf session list --needs-me` surface unresolved Asks and current reviews even beneath collapsed Tasks. Confirmed exited orphan conversations leave the working set while retaining history; Task/Wave conversations, primary Sessions and pending obligations are preserved.\n- `lf session ensure` returns the repository’s ongoing conversation; add `-w <wave>` for a Wave conversation. `lf session replace SESSION` starts a successor while retaining completed history.\n- Flow previews fold composed templates, and Task workspaces link interactive stages to their exact conversations. Automated steps, branches and repeats remain inspectable.\n\n## Inspect plans before starting, and reorganize without losing work\n\nPlanning lookup no longer depends on a local execution record. Existing branches and nested Waves can keep their identity and progress as work is adopted or reorganized.\n\n- `lf task status <issue> --json` reports planning, freshness, errors and optional execution without allocating a worktree. Project-less issues remain inspectable, and failed refreshes retain the last successful observation.\n- Checkout can adopt a Linear branch, reuse a dirty worktree or fetch an open PR’s branch. Repeated operations preserve the PR and captured Flow cursor. Managed continuation rechecks planning and pauses on unavailable or incompatible plans without discarding progress.\n- Nested Waves inherit repository and ancestor context. Durable `id:` fields preserve Wave identity and Project/Task links across renames and reparenting; commit those fields and retain them when moving directories.\n- Chapter sweeps, planning refresh and Wave sync skip Projects known to belong exclusively to other Teams. Missing or conflicting ownership still needs resolution, but unrelated foreign Projects no longer stop the repository’s work.\n\n## Keep delivery moving between visits\n\nScheduled repository checks resume enrolled Tasks and settle verified merges while Desktop is closed. CI repair has a separate watcher, so delivery can be monitored from Desktop, a terminal or an installed service.\n\n- `lf land` records delivery and returns; a Flow’s landing step still waits for verified merge before advancing. `lf task reconcile` checks Tasks and landings once, while `lf pr reconcile` checks delivery alone.\n- Per-Home minute checks respect reviews, live work and bounded retries. Historical Tasks remain unenrolled until selected. Background progress and `lf task automation --json` show schedule coverage, errors, blockers and pending delivery.\n- Desktop starts a CI watcher for each open repository. `lf ci watch` also supports one-pass polling, service installation and status inspection, with rate-limit backoff and duplicate-repair prevention.\n- Ordinary CI repairs require both a recorded landing and an active watcher. Scheduled reconciliation records failures and settles merges but does not start those repairs; without a watcher, failed ordinary landings wait. Release-owned landings retain their repair path, and failing PRs without recorded landings are reported only.\n\n## See and control what agents receive\n\nLaunch budgets are configurable and inspectable, and recorded context can be broken down by source. The final defaults preserve more memory while reducing scratch input; complete excerpted files remain available on disk.\n\n- `lf context --skill implement` previews local headless input without launching a provider or refreshing Linear. Reports show original and submitted usage, effective limits and configuration sources. Overrides resolve from Wave frontmatter, repository config, personal config, then defaults.\n- Memory defaults are **16,000 tokens / 128 KiB**, shared across repository, ancestor and selected Wave memory. Scratch defaults are **12,000 tokens / 96 KiB**. Total-input limits remain **64,000 tokens / 512 KiB**.\n- Wave documents reach IDE launches through assembled prompts, and repeated document sources are deduplicated. `realign` consults child memories for shared lessons and curates oversized memory without shrinking files merely because they are large but within budget.\n- `lf usage --context` and Desktop Session history show source breakdowns and budget overruns. Missing measurements stay unknown. Counts mix local and provider tokenizers; carried context is an estimate and is unavailable for Codex.\n- `lf usage --weekly` reports input/output ratios, input size, median and p90 turn duration, and long silences within completed turns. Unfiltered reports publish the latest complete week’s metrics; Wave, Project and Task filters remain read-only.\n- `lf usage --binds` compares recorded attribution with hypothetical whole-conversation attribution. Binding still leaves earlier usage with its original owner; this report does not reassign it.\n\n## Operational notes\n\n- **One Home, one database:** ordinary source CLI commands forward to the installed CLI and main `~/.lf` Home. An explicit `LF_HOME` selects an isolated experiment inherited by children. Each Home uses `loopflow.db`; `LF_DB_PATH` and retired `LF_CONTROL_*` overrides are removed. Existing side stores and custom database paths are not imported or migrated.\n- **Experimental schemas:** use a fresh experimental Home after schema changes, including for Homes containing the removed draft receipt ledger. Published installation retains snapshot validation, released-schema migrations and interrupted-install recovery; intermediate branch schemas are not an upgrade contract.\n- **CLI and JSON consumers:** commands are organized under their owners, with uniquely resolving shorthand such as `lf land`, `lf ps` and `lf top` retained. Task status JSON now uses a planning/execution envelope; Task snapshots replace `runs` and `runs_truncated` with `work`, Session records add `task_ids`, and Project-level sweep entries can have `issue: null`.\n- **Background operation:** scheduling uses macOS launchd and requires the Home’s user to remain logged in. Holding a Task or disabling its schedule prevents future automatic admissions; running work and existing GitHub merge requests continue. CI repair confirmation requires GraphQL quota. Watcher status is currently available through the CLI, without a dedicated Desktop view.\n- **Acceptance limits:** supplied PR evidence includes focused Rust, Swift and Python checks, native builds and a live GitHub polling pass, but does not establish a clean full matrix for the combined release. Live-provider adoption, repair and merge, installed Home acceptance, and full cross-Task retention remain unverified end to end. Context-report readers were exercised against real captures; weekly live-data validation remains outstanding.\n\n## Small changes\n\n- Repository conventions now live in one regular `AGENTS.md`; the repository’s `STYLE.md` and `CLAUDE.md` symlinks are removed. Providers load repository instructions natively, outside injected context.\n- The migration helper reuses the Task branch’s existing draft without changing its SQL. Edit that draft in place and test the released schema against the finished draft.\n- Newly started tmux servers and Session shells clear inherited execution context. Already-running tmux servers retain their previous environment.\n- Contributors can inventory recorded context and replay source-removal comparisons with `scripts/context_ablation.py`. The retained pilot does not establish equivalent code quality or reliable time/cost savings; replays consume provider usage.","source_limits":{"context_bytes":131072,"commits":256,"merged_prs":200,"files_per_change":100,"area_scopes":32,"name_bytes":256,"title_bytes":300,"path_bytes":512,"pr_body_bytes":4096,"decisions_bytes":16384,"previous_release_notes_bytes":16384,"release_notes_bytes":61440},"omissions":{"commits":0,"merged_prs":0,"commit_files":0,"pr_files":0,"area_scopes":0,"text_bytes":0,"decisions_bytes":0,"previous_release_notes_bytes":0}}